-- V1.8.5 — Rencontres entre clubs (docs/V185_RENCONTRES_CLUBS.md, docs/V185_SIMULATIONS.md). Applies after 20261127090000 (V1.8.4).
-- Two clubs of different sizes and disciplines play a private one- or two-week challenge with a limited contribution per person, first in
-- COOPERATION (both clubs aim together at a common score). The comparative format (« rencontre », the better rate leads) is implemented
-- but behind its own server flag, closed: it opens only if the cooperation pilot shows that members understand their score.
-- Built from bricks that already hold:
--   * The club and its roles (20261030090000): only club ADMINISTRATORS organise. An administrator of club A proposes (format, start
--     tomorrow to 28 days, 1 or 2 weeks, a tested pace); the club gets a one-time code that an administrator of club B — another account —
--     reads in a preview (rate-limited, never an error, so the limiter holds) and accepts or refuses before the start. Each side may stop:
--     before the start the meeting is cancelled, after it is abandoned with no result. One meeting at a time per club, as host or guest.
--   * EXPLICIT PARTICIPATION (as the club season, 20261127090000): nobody is added; each member of either club chooses to take part,
--     until the end of the second day. Leaving is final; leaving the club, or being removed from it, leaves the meeting (trigger).
--   * The measure is the ACTIVE DAY of the club season: a Paris day with at least 12 counted effort-minutes from CONFIRMED sessions only
--     (private.titan_confirmed_sessions), 90 a day at most, recorded during the participation. Every discipline is equal.
--   * THE SCORE: each participant's SHARE = active days per week of the pace × weeks of participation (prorated to the time spent,
--     rounded up: a withdrawal keeps the share of the time spent, so making the inactive leave never raises a rate). Each counts their
--     days UP TO THEIR OWN SHARE (cap 1 ×): a very active member never carries their club. A club's RATE = counted days ÷ sum of the shares,
--     in whole percent rounded down; it exists only with 3 participants still in (the confidentiality threshold of the club week).
--     Cooperation: COMMON SCORE = mean of the two rates (each club weighs half, whatever its size); reached at 60 %. Comparison: the
--     better rate leads; less than 5 points apart is a tie; two weeks only. The values are chosen by simulation (tools/simulate-club-match.mjs).
--   * CONFIDENTIALITY: the other club receives only a club name, a number of participants and a rate — never a name, a list of sessions,
--     a day or a presence. During the meeting every score is computed AS OF THE LAST PARIS MIDNIGHT (sessions dated and recorded before),
--     so nobody can see when a member trains; one reads one's own days live. One's own club also reads its counted total and goal.
--   * Same inputs, same result: the final score is computed as of the end (sessions dated and recorded before it) and frozen once in
--     the recap (status 'closed', phase 'closed' or 'short' when a club had fewer than 3 participants at the end); never recomputed.
--   * The pilot's measure: each participant may say whether the score was clear and whether they would play again (private.
--     titan_club_match_measure: meetings completed, misunderstandings, sides that want to play again; counts only).
--   * No XP, credit, title or ranking of people. Flags: screens.club_match (propose, accept, join; absent = closed) and
--     screens.club_match_versus (the comparative format; absent = closed). Refusing, leaving, stopping and answering always work.
--     Exported (« clubMatches ») and erased with the account; a meeting keeps its recap without its organisers (on delete set null).
-- Additive. The caller owns the transaction: never BEGIN/COMMIT here.
